TEXT -192 200 Left 2 ;V(N004)*1W/1V + CTRL/Click from 500.0ms to 501ms = -14.432kJ (Trafo)\nV(N007)*1W/1V + CTRL/Click from 500.0ms to 501ms = +7.22kJ (Load2)\nV(N031)*1W/1V + CTRL/Click from 500.0ms to 501ms = +7.22kJ (Load1)
TEXT -192 168 Left 2 ;The energy stored in the transformer element is for 40MW load \nabout:
TEXT 160 176 Left 2 ;The conservated (stored)  inductive energy of trafo (-14.432kJ)\nwork after switchoff in the load devices (7.22kJ+7.22kJ)\nTherefore in this example there is no voltagespike !!!!
TEXT 488 32 Left 2 ;The height of load \nmeans a full loaded \ntranformer
TEXT -192 256 Left 2 ;NOTE: The primary voltage has voltage spikes\nbecause the current through the switch changes too fast to zero\n(hard switching)
TEXT -32 112 Left 2 ;Hard switching:\ntoff=1u vt=0.9 vh=0
TEXT 80 176 Left 0 ;This load is only for\nleting the current flow after\nswitching off
TEXT 104 160 Left 2 ;Load1
