TEXT 104 152 Left 2 !.param  pn1=40e6
TEXT 264 -72 Left 2 ;Etrafo before 500ms:\nIntegral of Energy halvewave\nE=E1+E2+E3=1.5*E1\nE2,E3=0.25*E1
TEXT -192 232 Left 2 ;See plot file: Inductive_Energy_HighLoaded_Transformer_with_Energymeter_gt_500ms.plt
TEXT 264 -88 Left 2 ;V(N001)*1W/1V + CTRL/Click from 490.697ms to 495.697ms = 14.355kJ (Trafo)
TEXT 264 -104 Left 2 ;See plot file: Inductive_Energy_HighLoaded_Transformer_with_Energymeter_lt_500ms.plt
TEXT 392 -72 Left 2 ;HINT: With a transformer of rotating vector group e.g. YD11\nthis energy measurement doesn't work because\nThe energy delivered per phase is varying \ne.g. Energy of Phase1 primary is not equal Energy\nof Phase1 secondary !!!!!!\nOnly the energy of the sum of the primary phases\nand the sum of the secondary phases is equal\nTo handle this always exchange the YD transformer\nwith a YY0 transformer with the same parameters
TEXT -40 -96 Left 2 ;Works only with \nvector group 0 (e.g.YY0)\nThat means if you want to measure the\nstored energy of a circuit with e.g Yd5 \ntransformer you have to exchange Yd5 \nwith Yy0 (same transformer paramters)
TEXT 336 224 Left 2 ;NOTE: Comparing to the example with the shorted transformer\nthe stored energy is 14.4kJ to 331kJ !!!
